240
00:39:24,070 --> 00:39:26,364
Why did you bring me here?

241
00:39:30,326 --> 00:39:31,786
No! What are you doing?

242
00:39:31,952 --> 00:39:33,496
Hey, stop!

243
00:39:33,746 --> 00:39:35,039
Get away from it! Stop!

244
00:39:42,755 --> 00:39:45,299
Sarah Connor was cremated in Mexico.

245
00:39:45,466 --> 00:39:47,760
Her friends scattered her ashes 
in the sea.

246
00:39:48,135 --> 00:39:51,388
They stored these weapons 
in accordance with her will.

247
00:39:53,991 --> 00:39:56,536
[Edit: Sarah / leukemia / Baja]

248
00:39:56,936 --> 00:39:58,979
"Every day after this one is a gift. "

249
00:39:59,188 --> 00:40:02,024
She told me, "We made it. We're free. "

250
00:40:04,860 --> 00:40:07,488
But I never really believed that.

251
00:40:10,533 --> 00:40:12,952
I guess she didn't either.

252
00:40:14,745 --> 00:40:18,457
You know you were about 
the closest thing to a father I ever had?

253
00:40:19,625 --> 00:40:21,419
How pathetic is that?

254
00:40:22,962 --> 00:40:24,171
Out of my way!

255
00:40:27,550 --> 00:40:29,552
My mission is to protect you.

256
00:40:30,428 --> 00:40:31,720
That's enough.

257
00:40:33,305 --> 00:40:36,725
Move or I'll do it! 
I swear I will! I'll shoot you!

258
00:40:36,725 --> 00:40:40,062
Go ahead. See what happens.

259
00:40:54,827 --> 00:40:56,495
Don't do that.

260
00:40:58,581 --> 00:41:00,624
Oh, my God.

261
00:41:06,755 --> 00:41:10,092
This is the police. 
We have the building surrounded.

262
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:12,428
Release your hostage!

263
00:41:31,803 --> 00:41:33,424
[Edit: TX / John “not the one you want” psych]

264
00:41:33,824 --> 00:41:35,868
Perps still holed up?

265
00:41:36,994 --> 00:41:38,078
Gotcha.

266
00:41:38,245 --> 00:41:40,789
Good news. Your fiancee's okay.

267
00:41:40,956 --> 00:41:42,041
Where is she?

268
00:41:42,208 --> 00:41:44,710
Greenlawn Cemetery, 
up off the 5 freeway.

269
00:41:44,919 --> 00:41:48,881
It's right by the desert. 
But they're gonna bring her back to the-

270
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,301
Oh, my God! Oh, my dear Jesus! God!

271
00:42:16,158 --> 00:42:19,620
You're safe now. They can't hurt you.

272
00:42:20,204 --> 00:42:23,374
Kate, my name is Dr. Silberman.

273
00:42:23,540 --> 00:42:26,877
I'm a post-trauma counselor 
for the sheriff's department.

274
00:42:27,044 --> 00:42:29,046
How are you feeling?

275
00:42:29,838 --> 00:42:31,840
He's not human.

276
00:42:32,174 --> 00:42:36,345
He's really not human.

277
00:42:38,764 --> 00:42:42,226
I know what it's like to be 
in a hostage situation.

278
00:42:42,434 --> 00:42:44,478
I've been there myself.

279
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:47,773
The fear, the adrenaline.

280
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:51,860
You find yourself imagining things.

281
00:42:52,403 --> 00:42:54,947
Impossible things.

282
00:42:55,656 --> 00:42:57,866
Crazy things.

283
00:42:59,118 --> 00:43:01,370
Insane things.

284
00:43:03,330 --> 00:43:06,208
Take years to get over it.

285
00:43:07,459 --> 00:43:09,878
- Go, go, go! 
- Move it!

286
00:43:15,551 --> 00:43:16,844
Drop your weapon!

287
00:43:20,639 --> 00:43:22,641
And the coffin!

288
00:43:24,977 --> 00:43:27,479
Take him down! Take him down!

289
00:44:08,395 --> 00:44:10,439
Resume fire!

290
00:44:17,529 --> 00:44:19,907
We must reacquire Katherine Brewster.

291
00:44:20,699 --> 00:44:23,619
Why? What makes her 
so goddamn important?

292
00:44:23,786 --> 00:44:28,123
Through her, you contact remnants of the 
military and learn how to fight Skynet...

293
00:44:28,415 --> 00:44:30,793
...forming the core 
of the Resistance.

294
00:44:31,845 --> 00:44:35,345
[Edit: Future kids / “She's your wife.”]

295
00:44:35,495 --> 00:44:43,316
Cringy machine-lecture beats (“You’ll find a way to destroy her” — did he read the script?), anti-Terminator Terminator gag, destiny / breeding-age / “she’s your wife” / spouse–second-in-command dumps, “fuck my destiny”

296
00:44:43,466 --> 00:44:46,074
gun-to-head, Sarah leukemia/Baja speech, Crystal Peak “nothing here” flop

297
00:45:29,017 --> 00:45:30,727
Get in!

298
00:45:30,894 --> 00:45:32,396
Do you want to live? Come on!

299
00:45:54,752 --> 00:45:58,130
- It was Scott! How could it be Scott? 
- Your fiance?

300
00:45:58,297 --> 00:46:02,301
The T-X is polymimetic, 
able to take the form of anything it touches.

301
00:46:03,093 --> 00:46:05,137
Your fiance is dead.

302
00:46:29,703 --> 00:46:30,746
Oh, my God!

303
00:46:36,418 --> 00:46:37,544
Do something!

304
00:47:08,575 --> 00:47:10,285
Get down.

305
00:47:32,766 --> 00:47:35,018
We need a new vehicle.

306
00:48:57,935 --> 00:48:59,478
Hey, come on.

307
00:48:59,645 --> 00:49:01,772
We gotta keep moving.

308
00:49:03,941 --> 00:49:06,526
She killed Scott because of me.

309
00:49:13,283 --> 00:49:15,577
Look, I know this won't help...

310
00:49:17,788 --> 00:49:23,377
...but sometimes things happen 
that we just can't change.

311
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:28,882
It's not your fault.

312
00:49:38,225 --> 00:49:41,687
So this Terminatrix, how many others 
does she have on her hit list?

313
00:49:41,737 --> 00:49:43,237
[Edit: Breeding-age / pair-bonding]

314
00:49:43,237 --> 00:49:46,775
Twenty-two. Anderson, Elizabeth. 
Anderson, William.

315
00:49:46,942 --> 00:49:49,695
Barrera, Jose. Brewster, Robert.

316
00:49:49,861 --> 00:49:51,154
My father?

317
00:49:51,321 --> 00:49:56,326
Having failed to acquire its primary target, 
T- X will resume its default program.

318
00:49:56,493 --> 00:50:00,580
- She's gonna kill my father too? 
- There's a high probability.

319
00:50:01,331 --> 00:50:03,667
- No. 
- Who is he? What does he do?

320
00:50:03,834 --> 00:50:08,338
He's in the Air Force. Weapon design, 
secret stuff. I don't know, exactly.

321
00:50:08,547 --> 00:50:12,300
General Robert Brewster 
is program director of CRS...

322
00:50:12,467 --> 00:50:16,388
...Cyber Research Systems, 
autonomous weapons division.

323
00:50:16,555 --> 00:50:19,474
Skynet. You're talking about Skynet.

324
00:50:19,641 --> 00:50:23,937
Skynet is one of the digital defense systems 
developed under Brewster.

325
00:50:24,104 --> 00:50:25,605
Oh, God.

326
00:50:26,022 --> 00:50:29,234
Oh, my God. Of course.

327
00:50:29,609 --> 00:50:31,069
It all makes sense now.

328
00:50:31,945 --> 00:50:35,365
If you hadn't come back when I was a kid, 
changed everything...

329
00:50:35,532 --> 00:50:39,619
...she and I would have gotten together 
then. I would have met her father.

330
00:50:39,995 --> 00:50:42,414
- Don't you see? 
- I don't understand.

331
00:50:42,581 --> 00:50:46,543
Your father. 
This is all about your father.

332
00:50:46,710 --> 00:50:51,298
He's the key. He always was. Your father 
is the one who can shut Skynet down.

333
00:50:52,716 --> 00:50:55,177
He's the only one who ever could.

334
00:50:57,053 --> 00:50:59,222
We have to get to him 
before the T-X does.

335
00:50:59,431 --> 00:51:03,935
- Negative. I cannot jeopardize my mission. 
- This is your mission, to save people!

336
00:51:04,102 --> 00:51:08,064
My mission is to ensure the survival 
of John Connor and Katherine Brewster.

337
00:51:08,815 --> 00:51:11,109
I am giving you an order.

338
00:51:11,276 --> 00:51:13,862
I am not programmed 
to follow your orders.

339
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:17,115
- After the nuclear war, you both- 
- Nuclear war?!

340
00:51:17,282 --> 00:51:20,368
There doesn't have to be a war! 
We can stop it!

341
00:51:20,535 --> 00:51:22,746
There is insufficient time.

342
00:51:22,913 --> 00:51:27,084
The first launch sequences 
will be initiated at 6:18 p. m.

343
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:29,002
- What, today? 
- Affirmative.

344
00:51:29,169 --> 00:51:31,880
John, what is he saying?

345
00:51:33,006 --> 00:51:35,008
Judgment Day.

346
00:51:36,384 --> 00:51:38,595
The end of the world.

347
00:51:39,971 --> 00:51:41,932
It's today, three hours from now.

348
00:51:42,390 --> 00:51:44,392
Two hours and 53 minutes.

349
00:51:44,601 --> 00:51:49,648
We must continue south into Mexico 
to escape the primary blast zones.

350
00:51:50,398 --> 00:51:53,193
No, we have to get to her dad.

351
00:51:54,861 --> 00:51:58,782
The Mojave area will sustain 
significant nuclear fallout.

352
00:51:58,949 --> 00:52:00,575
You will not survive.

353
00:52:01,409 --> 00:52:05,747
You mean we go run and hide somewhere 
in a hole while the bombs fall?

354
00:52:06,623 --> 00:52:07,082
It is your destiny.

355
00:52:09,793 --> 00:52:14,089
Please do what he says. 
You have to save my father!

356
00:52:14,489 --> 00:52:17,901
[Edit: “Fuck my destiny” / gun-to-head]

357
00:52:18,301 --> 00:52:21,805
We can reach CRS 
in approximately one hour...

358
00:52:22,013 --> 00:52:24,766
...depending on traffic conditions.

359
00:52:25,166 --> 00:52:27,566
cannot self-terminate; 83% he won’t pull the trigger.

360
00:52:27,716 --> 00:52:35,537
Cringy machine-lecture beats (“You’ll find a way to destroy her” — did he read the script?), anti-Terminator Terminator gag, destiny / breeding-age / “she’s your wife” / spouse–second-in-command dumps, “fuck my destiny”

361
00:52:35,687 --> 00:52:38,295
gun-to-head, Sarah leukemia/Baja speech, Crystal Peak “nothing here” flop

362
00:52:40,574 --> 00:52:42,242
I can't get a line.

363
00:52:45,328 --> 00:52:47,163
The whole cell network is down.

364
00:52:47,330 --> 00:52:50,250
Skynet is assuming control 
over global communications...

365
00:52:50,417 --> 00:52:52,752
...in preparation for its attack.

366
00:52:52,919 --> 00:52:57,090
So if this war is between people 
and machines...

367
00:52:57,382 --> 00:52:59,634
...why are you on our side?

368
00:52:59,801 --> 00:53:03,722
The Resistance captured me 
and reprogrammed my CPU.

369
00:53:03,889 --> 00:53:07,392
I was originally designed 
for assassination missions.

370
00:53:10,353 --> 00:53:11,855
So...

371
00:53:12,189 --> 00:53:16,067
...you don't really care 
if this mission succeeds or not.

372
00:53:16,651 --> 00:53:20,614
If we get killed, 
does that mean anything to you?

373
00:53:20,780 --> 00:53:24,034
If you were to die, 
I will become useless.

374
00:53:24,200 --> 00:53:27,329
There will be no reason for me to exist.

375
00:53:33,001 --> 00:53:35,045
Thank you for doing this.

376
00:53:35,212 --> 00:53:37,214
Your gratitude is not required.

377
00:53:37,923 --> 00:53:40,342
I am programmed 
to follow your commands.

378
00:53:41,343 --> 00:53:42,719
Her commands?

379
00:53:42,886 --> 00:53:48,266
Katherine Brewster had me reactivated and 
sent through the time displacement field.

380
00:53:48,266 --> 00:53:50,268
Why didn't I send you back?

381
00:53:50,318 --> 00:53:51,818
[Edit: Kate = spouse / second-in-command]

382
00:53:51,818 --> 00:53:52,729
I am not authorized 
to answer your question.

383
00:53:54,522 --> 00:53:57,984
- Why didn't he send you back? 
- He was dead.

384
00:53:58,384 --> 00:54:02,172
future-role dump + “you're not exactly my type.” Cringy machine-lecture beats (“You’ll find a way to destroy her” — did he read the script?), anti-Terminator Terminator gag, destiny / breeding-age / “she’s your wife” /

385
00:54:02,572 --> 00:54:04,282
Well, that sucks.

386
00:54:05,200 --> 00:54:09,120
- Humans inevitably die. 
- Yeah, I know.

387
00:54:10,038 --> 00:54:12,123
So how does it-? No.

388
00:54:12,582 --> 00:54:15,377
Maybe I don't want to know.

389
00:54:16,962 --> 00:54:18,463
How does he die?

390
00:54:19,172 --> 00:54:22,968
John Connor was terminated 
on July 4th, 2032.

391
00:54:23,134 --> 00:54:27,013
I was selected for the emotional attachment 
he had for my model number...

392
00:54:27,222 --> 00:54:31,476
...due to his boyhood experiences. 
This aided in my infiltration.

393
00:54:32,435 --> 00:54:34,062
What are you saying?

394
00:54:35,855 --> 00:54:38,191
I killed you.

395
00:54:50,453 --> 00:54:55,458
This has to be a mistake. As of 1100 hours, 
all primary military systems were secure.

396
00:54:55,625 --> 00:54:59,713
They were. Only the civilian sector 
was affected. Internet, air traffic.

397
00:54:59,879 --> 00:55:02,674
Minutes ago, guidance computers 
at Vandenberg crashed.

398
00:55:02,841 --> 00:55:05,552
We thought it was an error. 
It looks like the virus.

399
00:55:05,719 --> 00:55:09,973
- Early warning in Alaska is down. 
- Satellite signals are scrambled.

400
00:55:10,140 --> 00:55:13,018
What about the missile silos, the subs?

401
00:55:14,019 --> 00:55:16,229
We've lost contact.

402
00:55:16,730 --> 00:55:20,150
You're saying this country 
is completely open to attack.

403
00:55:20,316 --> 00:55:23,153
Theoretically, we could be 
under attack already.

404
00:55:23,319 --> 00:55:28,783
Who's doing this? A foreign power 
or some computer hacker in his garage?

405
00:55:28,950 --> 00:55:31,077
We can't trace the virus 
or pin it down.

406
00:55:31,244 --> 00:55:35,373
It keeps growing and changing, 
like it has a mind of its own.

407
00:55:35,915 --> 00:55:37,667
This can't be happening.

408
00:55:37,834 --> 00:55:42,047
The Pentagon's on the secure line. 
It's the chairman.

409
00:55:45,300 --> 00:55:47,218
All right.

410
00:56:01,649 --> 00:56:03,568
Look...

411
00:56:03,943 --> 00:56:05,862
...none of this is gonna happen.

412
00:56:06,488 --> 00:56:11,910
We get to your dad, get him to pull the plug 
on Skynet. The bombs won't fall.

413
00:56:14,287 --> 00:56:17,123
He won't have to kill me someday.

414
00:56:17,874 --> 00:56:20,210
He'll never even exist.

415
00:56:21,878 --> 00:56:27,217
You and I, we can 
just go our separate ways.

416
00:56:30,760 --> 00:56:34,260
[Edit: Kripke basement (again) + levity]

417
00:56:34,410 --> 00:56:42,089
first-kiss reminisce; “Your levity is good… fear of death.” Junkies line, obnoxious cat-woman clinic dialogue (programming that only makes you want her dead), Mike Kripke’s basement reminisce (and the later rematch)

418
00:56:52,742 --> 00:56:55,370
We're hoping you have a solution for us.

419
00:56:55,537 --> 00:56:59,332
I know, sir, but Skynet is not ready 
for a system-wide connection.

420
00:56:59,499 --> 00:57:02,460
That's not what your civilian 
counterparts there told me.

421
00:57:02,627 --> 00:57:04,921
They say we can stop this damn virus.

422
00:57:05,088 --> 00:57:08,591
I understand there's a certain amount 
of performance anxiety...

423
00:57:08,758 --> 00:57:12,095
...but your boys say if we plug Skynet 
into all of our systems...

424
00:57:12,262 --> 00:57:16,349
...it'll squash this thing and give me back 
control of my military.

425
00:57:16,516 --> 00:57:19,018
Mr. Chairman, I need 
to make myself very clear.

426
00:57:19,185 --> 00:57:22,605
If we uplink now, Skynet will be 
in control of your military.

427
00:57:22,772 --> 00:57:26,818
But you'll be in control of Skynet, right?

428
00:57:27,152 --> 00:57:29,279
That is correct, sir.

429
00:57:29,446 --> 00:57:30,822
Then do it.

430
00:57:30,989 --> 00:57:33,741
And Brewster, if this thing works...

431
00:57:33,908 --> 00:57:37,287
...you'll get all the funding 
you'll ever need.

432
00:57:38,246 --> 00:57:40,165
Yes, sir.

433
00:58:48,775 --> 00:58:50,401
Sir?

434
00:58:51,653 --> 00:58:53,404
Shall I?

435
00:58:54,948 --> 00:58:56,491
No.

436
00:58:57,617 --> 00:58:59,827
It's my job now.

437
00:59:14,300 --> 00:59:17,345
- Skynet Defense System activated. 
- We're in.

438
00:59:17,512 --> 00:59:20,723
We're past the firewalls, local 
defense nets, Minutemen, subs.

439
00:59:20,890 --> 00:59:25,019
Skynet's fully operational, 
processing at 60 teraflops a second.

440
00:59:25,228 --> 00:59:29,065
It should take less than a minute 
to find the virus and kill it.

441
00:59:30,191 --> 00:59:33,027
Let's pray to God this works.

442
00:59:39,284 --> 00:59:40,451
Power failure?

443
00:59:40,618 --> 00:59:42,954
No. I don't know what it is.

444
00:59:54,007 --> 00:59:56,426
What the hell is going on?

445
00:59:56,593 --> 00:59:57,635
Daddy!

446
00:59:58,177 --> 00:59:59,721
What are you doing here?

447
01:00:06,102 --> 01:00:08,896
Daddy! Get away from it!

448
01:00:12,692 --> 01:00:14,235
Watch out!

449
01:00:31,461 --> 01:00:33,379
Daddy, don't move.

450
01:00:37,759 --> 01:00:39,469
She'll be back.

451
01:00:40,136 --> 01:00:42,096
We have to shut down Skynet.

452
01:00:42,305 --> 01:00:44,932
Where's the system core? 
In this building?

453
01:00:45,099 --> 01:00:48,895
Skynet. The virus has infected Skynet.

454
01:00:49,062 --> 01:00:52,190
Skynet is the virus! 
It's why everything's falling apart!

455
01:00:52,357 --> 01:00:54,484
Skynet has become self-aware.

456
01:00:54,651 --> 01:00:58,279
In one hour it will initiate 
a massive nuclear attack on its enemy.

457
01:00:58,488 --> 01:00:59,572
What enemy?

458
01:01:00,156 --> 01:01:01,574
Us!

459
01:01:01,741 --> 01:01:03,076
Humans.

460
01:01:12,168 --> 01:01:15,463
Oh, God! It's the machines. 
They're starting to take over.

461
01:01:15,630 --> 01:01:19,092
My office, on this floor, 
we have to get there.

462
01:01:20,259 --> 01:01:22,512
The access codes are in my safe.

463
01:02:41,299 --> 01:02:44,677
- Why are they killing everyone? 
- To destroy any possible threat to Skynet.

464
01:02:44,677 --> 01:02:47,346
Which ones are the codes?

465
01:02:47,513 --> 01:02:49,348
Red envelope.

466
01:02:53,144 --> 01:02:56,981
Crystal Peak. You have 
to get to Crystal Peak.

467
01:02:57,148 --> 01:02:59,317
- What is he saying? 
- Crystal Peak.

468
01:02:59,484 --> 01:03:02,153
A hardened facility 
in the Sierra Nevada mountains.

469
01:03:02,320 --> 01:03:06,115
Fifty-two miles northeast, 
bearing 0.5 degrees.

470
01:03:06,282 --> 01:03:07,950
That's the system core?

471
01:03:08,534 --> 01:03:10,661
It's your only chance.

472
01:03:10,828 --> 01:03:15,792
You'll need a plane. The particle accelerator 
leads to the runway.

473
01:03:17,794 --> 01:03:19,587
Take care of my daughter.

474
01:03:21,964 --> 01:03:25,384
Oh, Katie, I am sorry.

475
01:03:25,551 --> 01:03:28,846
I opened Pandora's box.

476
01:03:30,014 --> 01:03:31,015
Get down!

477
01:03:47,448 --> 01:03:49,825
There's nothing you can do. Come on.

478
01:03:49,992 --> 01:03:52,078
We must go. It is not safe here.

479
01:03:52,828 --> 01:03:55,289
Kate, we have to go.

480
01:03:55,498 --> 01:03:59,168
Kate! He wanted you to come with me.

481
01:03:59,418 --> 01:04:03,548
He wanted us to shut Skynet down. 
Come on.

482
01:04:05,341 --> 01:04:06,759
Come on.

483
01:04:18,729 --> 01:04:20,356
Run!

484
01:05:54,992 --> 01:05:56,577
Let's go.

485
01:07:07,982 --> 01:07:10,818
That's it. We can follow it 
out to the runway.

486
01:07:11,026 --> 01:07:12,737
Come on.

487
01:08:10,240 --> 01:08:13,740
[Edit: “You remind me of my mother.”]

488
01:08:23,724 --> 01:08:26,185
Oh, God. She's coming.

489
01:08:29,730 --> 01:08:31,607
What are you doing?

490
01:08:32,691 --> 01:08:33,734
Powering up.

491
01:08:38,906 --> 01:08:40,032
Come on.

492
01:09:50,644 --> 01:09:52,021
It's working.

493
01:09:56,643 --> 01:09:59,212
[Edit: “Just die, you bitch!”]

494
01:09:59,612 --> 01:10:01,322
Come on.

495
01:11:17,523 --> 01:11:20,317
There's my father's plane. 
I trained on it.

496
01:11:31,370 --> 01:11:33,580
Yes! He made it.

497
01:11:35,541 --> 01:11:37,543
Get away from me.

498
01:11:40,045 --> 01:11:41,046
Leave!

499
01:11:42,798 --> 01:11:43,924
Now!

500
01:11:44,383 --> 01:11:45,551
Let's go!

501
01:11:50,514 --> 01:11:53,600
- The master's on. Throttle's set. 
- Come on. Let's go.

502
01:11:59,606 --> 01:12:02,651
Oh, please. You can't do this.

503
01:12:02,818 --> 01:12:04,445
I have no choice.

504
01:12:05,362 --> 01:12:07,698
The T-X...

505
01:12:07,990 --> 01:12:10,367
...has corrupted my system.

506
01:12:14,038 --> 01:12:17,041
You can't kill a human being. 
You said so yourself.

507
01:12:17,207 --> 01:12:19,084
Let him go!

508
01:12:23,756 --> 01:12:25,549
You're fighting it right now.

509
01:12:26,425 --> 01:12:28,510
My CPU is intact.

510
01:12:29,094 --> 01:12:32,890
But I cannot control my other functions.

511
01:12:33,057 --> 01:12:36,685
You don't have to do this. 
You don't want to do this!

512
01:12:37,186 --> 01:12:41,190
Desire is irrelevant.

513
01:12:41,398 --> 01:12:43,942
I am a machine.

514
01:13:00,542 --> 01:13:02,211
What is your mission?

515
01:13:03,962 --> 01:13:07,508
To ensure the survival of John Connor...

516
01:13:07,674 --> 01:13:09,718
...and Katherine Brewster.

517
01:13:15,057 --> 01:13:18,268
You are about to fail that mission!

518
01:13:25,150 --> 01:13:27,945
I can- I cannot.

519
01:13:29,029 --> 01:13:31,156
You know what you have to do.

520
01:13:33,117 --> 01:13:35,702
You know my destiny.

521
01:13:40,332 --> 01:13:41,500
I have to live.

522
01:14:22,207 --> 01:14:24,751
- Are you okay? 
- What happened?

523
01:14:24,918 --> 01:14:27,546
He couldn't do it. 
He shut himself down.

524
01:14:31,300 --> 01:14:33,886
- Can you fly? 
- Yeah.

525
01:15:01,288 --> 01:15:02,748
Okay. 015 degrees...

526
01:15:02,748 --> 01:15:07,878
...52 miles, our max air speed 
is about 160.

527
01:15:08,086 --> 01:15:10,464
We've got 32 minutes.

528
01:15:10,631 --> 01:15:12,466
It's just you and me now.

529
01:15:12,633 --> 01:15:15,093
What if we can't stop it?

530
01:15:15,719 --> 01:15:19,348
There's enough C-4 here 
to take out 10 supercomputers.

531
01:15:19,765 --> 01:15:22,100
We're gonna make it, Kate.

532
01:15:23,310 --> 01:15:25,687
The future is up to us.

533
01:15:32,110 --> 01:15:34,363
That's gotta be it.

534
01:16:37,509 --> 01:16:40,596
Skynet. There may be more of them.

535
01:16:45,767 --> 01:16:47,561
Come on.

536
01:17:01,783 --> 01:17:04,953
I think this is some kind of blast door.

537
01:17:08,081 --> 01:17:10,751
There's no way 
we can blow through this thing.

538
01:17:12,002 --> 01:17:13,003
John, look.

539
01:17:16,006 --> 01:17:17,424
Now what?

540
01:17:20,260 --> 01:17:22,596
It's a code prompt.

541
01:17:29,728 --> 01:17:32,773
Type in "Dakota 775."

542
01:17:37,027 --> 01:17:39,279
"Red 176."

543
01:18:00,300 --> 01:18:02,636
Come on! 
We gotta get this thing open.

544
01:18:02,886 --> 01:18:04,721
Here. It's "Avalon 412."

545
01:18:05,639 --> 01:18:06,973
Put it in!

546
01:18:41,341 --> 01:18:42,759
Come on!

547
01:18:58,358 --> 01:19:00,777
I'm back.

548
01:19:16,209 --> 01:19:18,378
Go! Now!

549
01:19:18,962 --> 01:19:19,963
Come on!

550
01:19:43,069 --> 01:19:45,405
- Thank you. 
- We'll meet again.

551
01:19:45,655 --> 01:19:46,823
Go!

552
01:19:47,991 --> 01:19:48,992
Come on!

553
01:20:31,993 --> 01:20:33,537
You are terminated.

554
01:21:04,150 --> 01:21:05,485
The elevator.

555
01:21:12,075 --> 01:21:14,494
I'll set the detonator for five minutes.

556
01:21:14,995 --> 01:21:17,414
That should give us enough time 
to get back up.

557
01:21:48,778 --> 01:21:50,530
What is this place?

558
01:22:31,237 --> 01:22:33,740
These computers are 30 years old.

559
01:22:42,248 --> 01:22:44,084
This isn't Skynet.

560
01:22:48,755 --> 01:22:50,590
There's nothing here.

561
01:22:55,762 --> 01:22:58,598
This is a fallout shelter for VIPs.

562
01:23:00,433 --> 01:23:02,769
Only they never got the warning.

563
01:23:07,737 --> 01:23:11,237
[Edit: Crystal Peak empty]

564
01:23:11,387 --> 01:23:16,675
“Goddamn it!” / “There's nothing here!” Cringy machine-lecture beats (“You’ll find a way to destroy her” — did he read the script?), anti-Terminator Terminator gag, destiny / breeding-age / “she’s your wife” /

565
01:23:17,075 --> 01:23:18,910
Why didn't he tell us?

566
01:23:19,310 --> 01:23:21,847
spouse–second-in-command dumps, “fuck my destiny” gun-to-head, Sarah leukemia/Baja speech, Crystal Peak “nothing here” flop

567
01:23:22,247 --> 01:23:24,666
Why did he lead us down here?

568
01:23:30,422 --> 01:23:32,090
To live.

569
01:23:33,258 --> 01:23:35,260
That was his mission.

570
01:23:49,107 --> 01:23:50,358
There was never any stopping it.

571
01:23:54,946 --> 01:23:56,281
John...

572
01:23:57,615 --> 01:23:59,284
...we could just...

573
01:24:00,118 --> 01:24:01,453
...let it go.

574
01:24:04,289 --> 01:24:05,623
Hello?

575
01:24:06,416 --> 01:24:08,626
Hello? Can somebody hear me?

576
01:24:09,711 --> 01:24:11,546
This is Montana Civil Defense.

577
01:24:12,213 --> 01:24:15,300
Somebody please come in.

578
01:24:15,800 --> 01:24:17,469
Is there anybody there?

579
01:24:17,802 --> 01:24:20,805
Anyone reading me? Over.

580
01:24:21,973 --> 01:24:26,227
Rumors about a launch sequence. 
Command and control have broken down.

581
01:24:27,479 --> 01:24:30,565
Is anyone receiving me? 
Somebody?

582
01:24:32,650 --> 01:24:34,652
Somebody please come in.

583
01:24:35,070 --> 01:24:36,404
Anybody out there?

584
01:24:36,654 --> 01:24:39,991
- This is SAC Nellis. We're under attack. 
- CQ? CQ?

585
01:24:40,241 --> 01:24:41,826
Is anybody there?

586
01:24:43,828 --> 01:24:47,499
This is John Connor at Crystal Peak.

587
01:24:48,416 --> 01:24:53,171
Connor? What the hell is happening? 
Who's in charge there?

588
01:25:00,011 --> 01:25:01,346
I am.

589
01:25:02,680 --> 01:25:05,016
Connor, can you help us?

590
01:25:05,350 --> 01:25:10,188
This is Montana Civil Defense. 
Where did you say you were again?

